# D-101, second site (REVIEW 7b9c60c, fable_pc's remark): a method whose RESULT is a named
# Structure, passed as a callable actual, is used as a value: its public prototype is written
# (l2_m_value_used).  l2_emit_public_sig reads the result through l2_sig_ret (the same dt_of_own(
# 1000+foreign)/l2_ft_of_own recovery l2_emit_formal already does for a formal, -137 part 2) --
# raw l2_m_ret[mi] would hand l2_emit_foreign_return an index past its table, the same class of
# failure D-101's formal half had. `applyBox` does not call `op` (a callable-result Structure
# through a callable formal is not callable yet, same boundary as unit_d101_struct_formal_value);
# this row is the prototype's.  Prototype recovers to `@: Lmx` (a graph handle), same shape
# l2_emit_foreign_return gives any graph result.
# Mutant: l2_sig_ret's own recovery reverted to a raw l2_m_ret[mi] read -- l2trans fails again,
# with no located diagnostic (an index past l2_foreign_const's table).
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box
fn: toBox (int: v) Box
end: toBox
fn: mk (int: v) Box
    b: merge Box
    b\v: v
    return: b
end: mk
fn: applyBox (toBox: op; int: n) int
    return: n
end: applyBox
fn: run () int
    return: applyBox(mk, 7)
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
